WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.830
Off parts of the North Pacific coast,
kelp grows in great forests of seaweed.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.770
Sea otters lived there too,
until people hunted them out.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.210
Where the otters were lost, the
kelp forests turned to bare rock.

4
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.420
Yet otters do not eat kelp.

5
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:22.030
So how can losing a few otters turn
a forest of seaweed into bare rock?

6
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.390
In this mission, you'll follow snowshoe
hares and lynx through a cycle of about

7
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.280
10 years, one peak always
trailing the other.

8
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.530
Then you'll fence out
predators, add extra food,

9
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.470
and find out what really limits the hares.

10
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.660
Your mission: explain how losing a few
otters can turn a forest of seaweed into

11
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:42.680
bare rock.
